<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Brazil's Cemig raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Brazil's Cemig raised.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- HSBC James Capel said on Friday it had upgraded its rating for Brazilian utility Companhia Energetica de Minas Gerais, or Cemig, to buy from long-term buy.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Cemig ranks among the top performers in Brazil this year, with an outstanding 37 percent share price appreciation, easily outperforming a market which is itself up 22 percent,&quot; the firm wrote in a report.</p>
<p>-- HSBC James Capel raised its price target for the shares to $56.</p>
<p>-- The shares were off 0.80 real to 47.20 reais in Sao Paulo.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
